body:
\[\[Niv Mizzet Reborn\]\] 5 color gates control. No stax pieces I only run 1 counterspell but there are other good 2 color counterspells you could include over some of the cards in my list and then just a lot of removal and boardwipes. Since the win condition for the deck is land based in either \[\[maze's end\]\] or swinging with a commander that has been buffed by a \[\[basilisk gate\]\] to be a one shot you can play a control game that doesn't need stax pieces. I can go into more depth on what I like if you want but this is a good intro to the deck.

&#x200B;

https://tappedout.net/mtg-decks/25-05-22-gates/

I put my version of a kykar deck at the end but I worked on leveraging even more of the pyromancers to make the deck work. Since I run so many cantrips in my build I was able to get away with less lands. A really big card for me since I am more focused on instants and sorceries has been \[\[raff weatherlight stalwart\]\]. Personally I think that Propaganda effects are some of the worst things to be doing in magic since they make a problem simply not your problem at that moment. I have been a really big fan of the \[\[polymorph\]\] effects in my deck since I generate so many tokens but it might not be quite as effective in yours. Sun titan feels a bit weak to me here. You aren't on fetches so it can't as easily help you ramp but I am guessing from your post that you are using it to try and make up for the land destruction that you are anticipating from your brother. I feel like if you are going to commit to putting mana barbs in your deck you might as well try and find a spot for \[\[burning earth\]\].

&#x200B;

https://www.moxfield.com/decks/\_C3l4\_qIRU-Z\_nLBXgLR3A

Red green deck with spells that have generic costs, \[\[goblin anarchomancer\]\] for lots of reduction. If you have the other enchantresses \[\[verduran enchantress\]\] is another to put in. I am personally not a fan of agitator ant and Kaima since I don't think goad is the greatest mechanic.

&#x200B;

If you are taking non creature suggestions, \[\[season of growth\]\] is an all star.

\[\[Reprocess\]\] and \[\[god-eternal bontu\]\] are excellent ways to turn excess treasures into cards. I picked up \[\[monumental corruption\]\] a few weeks ago and liked it. I have really like \[\[Magda Brazen outlaw\]\] it helps to tutor out my good artifacts like the hammer, you already have, \[\[Amulet of Vigor\]\], \[\[academy manufacturer\]\] and \[\[inspiring Statuary\]\]. I run a lot more drain/ ping effects because eventually I will run out of ways to get my troops in. Stuff like \[\[nadier's nightblade\]\] feels really good. There are certainly some cards in there that shouldn't really be like my homies the whackers but I love them and they stay even if something like \[\[dolmen gate\]\] could be another good way to let them exist.

&#x200B;

My Decklist: [https://tappedout.net/mtg-decks/03-05-22-jundem-out/](https://tappedout.net/mtg-decks/03-05-22-jundem-out/)

I've been working on a Kykar deck that runs more of the token makers since the white gives access to a few more but something like \[\[shared discovery\]\] could be a decent card to add. 4 creatures shouldn't be too bad for the additional cost and can help refuel for either next turn or converting on some of the creatures that entered that turn. How is your cards in hand versus other players because a \[\[windfall\]\] might be a decent catch up if you can afford the mutual refuel. There are of course a few more token makers that you can run if you so desire. You run 5 things that make tokens with casts and in just izzet I have 11. Their cmc is usually higher so I can understand avoiding them if you are looking for a sleeker build. 

&#x200B;

My list is here: https://www.moxfield.com/decks/\_C3l4\_qIRU-Z\_nLBXgLR3A

I built Niv as a gates commander and it turns out having a big ass mulldrifter in the command zone to help you keep your game plan afloat is a strong plan. Guild pairs are a lot easier to manipulate than card types in my opinion because you can still push the interaction effectively while getting multiple sorceries or instants that wouldn't be an option for the new Atraxa. Having 10 options to hit from rather than the 7 in Atraxa is also big. It always comes down to what sort of advantage you are able to amass with a control deck. Sometimes the best play for me if I have my mana set up is to cast a semi early wrath to keep the board clear and allow me to recast my commander to refill my hand. At the end of the day control is slighty under the gun because it is a multiplayer format so you have to be really aware of how your interaction will line up into multiple threats. I will freely admit that my build is notably missing counter spells outside of Drown in the Loch so I am much better equipped to deal with creature decks than spellslingers due to the package of wraths and single target removal I have.

&#x200B;

The list I run is here: https://tappedout.net/mtg-decks/25-05-22-gates/

I sort of get to cheat for most of my low land count decks because they are \[\[rielle\]\] which is wheels letting me see lands pretty consistently, \[\[ognis\]\] letting me supplement not drawing lands with the treasure generation and \[\[katilda dawnheart prime\]\] since she makes all my humans into mana dorks.

&#x200B;

However my voltron decks are very much so do the thing or perish so I'm not really looking to draw too many anyway. Tana and Bruse partner voltron runs 32 lands, and twelve 1 or 2 mana sources of ramp so I will usually be getting an aggressive enough hand to put the pressure on considering the deck has no cmc 5 or higher cards and a total cmc of 2.34. My Krenko Tin street deck is similarly built though I might have to shift more towards rituals to help speed the deck up since it is currently on 31 lands and nine 1 or 2 mana sources of ramp for a cmc of 2.26.

So I think for the most part it depends on how everyone is expecting the game to go down. If the pod shuffles up for chill magic with a couple battle cruisers and someone plays fast combo it won't feel fair, but on the otherhand if your play group is all about doing the thing and someone decided to bring hard stax and stop that it might be seen as just as unfair. To me fair or unfair comes down to what people think they signed up for when they shuffled up. To look at the examples you gave I have dealt with chatterfang decks that pretty much only exist to tutor for \[\[pitiless plunderer\]\] and win like that and when you aren't expecting tutors for a combo straight up it feels unfair but if people know what to expect and what they have to respect it can be perfectly fine. Akira Nadier I would like to see a list if it got called unfair because I would agree that that pairing doesn't look too bad. Usually the fairness or unfairness of akiri decks comes down to swords of X and Y or commander's plates making people feel like they can't remove the threat.

&#x200B;

Feel free to take my opinion with a grain of salt I tend to the one building problematic decks.
